From: Erwan Croze <erwan.croze@vates.tech>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: live (online) VDI resize on File/EXT/NFS/LVM SRs

Allow growing a VDI while it is attached to a running VM.

- FileSR/EXTSR/NFSSR and LVMSR: vdi_resize no longer refuses attached
  VDIs. When the VDI is attached, the tapdisk is paused, the VHD/QCOW2
  image (and the LV for LVMSR) is resized, then the tapdisk is unpaused
  with resize=True. On LVMSR, a thin-provisioned attached VDI stays
  inflated and the resized LV is refreshed on the slaves it is attached
  on.
- blktap2.VDI.tap_unpause / call_pluginhandler: new resize argument,
  forwarded to the tapdisk-pause plugin.
- tapdisk-pause: on unpause with resize=true, write "resize-device" in
  the xenstore backend/vbd3 node(s) whose params match the VDI path, so
  that tapback notifies the guest of the new size.
- VDI_RESIZE_ONLINE is advertised in the capabilities of the File, EXT,
  NFS and LVM SR drivers.
- vdi_resize is added to FileSR.OPS_EXCLUSIVE so it is serialised with
  the other exclusive SR operations.

Requires blktap >= 3.55.5-12.4.0.resizeonline.1 (tapdisk accepting a size
change on unpause).

Signed-off-by: Erwan Croze <erwan.croze@vates.tech>
